# Plugin workflow guidance

Use this rule when editing the plugin manifest, command docs, skill docs, install script, or Python parser.

## Current layout

- `plugin.json` currently defines one core skill and three commands
- `scripts/parse_ibt.py` is the standalone Python parser
- Reference docs live under `skills/iracing-gtp-engineer/references/`
- `install.ps1` copies the shipped files into the user plugin/skill directories

## Editing rules

- If you add commands, skills, or new supporting files, update `plugin.json` and `install.ps1` together
- Do not document paths like `references/*.md` at the plugin root unless those files actually exist there
- Keep command docs aligned with real files and supported workflows
- Prefer incremental additions over broad plugin-manifest expansion that the installer cannot yet provision

## Parser parity

- `gtp-telemetry/src/lib/ibt-parser.ts` is the browser port of the same domain logic
- When changing shared parsing assumptions, review both implementations for drift
- Keep channel names, unit assumptions, and fallback behavior explicit in docs
